  Read the matched-|move| block, not the raw rows. If an arm wins there,
  the wrap was costing real energy. If every arm collapses onto the same
  curve in |move|, then STEP SIZE is the only thing any of these knobs
  controls, the aliasing is real but performance-neutral, and it belongs
  in the mechanism section rather than the tuning section.
  This harness's null scale is 0.03-0.09; treat smaller gaps as zero.
